{"name":"Pink Explosion","hex":"#f56f88","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"explosion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A violent release of energy (sometimes mechanical, nuclear, or chemical); an act or instance of exploding.","The sound of an explosion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explosion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Explosion","blocks":[{"text":"An explosion is a rapid expansion in volume of a given amount of matter associated with an extreme outward release of energy, usually with the generation of high temperatures and release of high-pressure gases. Explosions may also be generated by a slower expansion that would normally not be forceful, but is not allowed to expand, so that when whatever is containing the expansion is broken by the pressure that builds as the matter inside tries to expand, the matter expands forcefully. An example of this is a volcanic eruption created by the expansion of magma in a magma chamber as it rises to the surface. Supersonic explosions created by high explosives are known as detonations and travel through shock waves. Subsonic explosions are created by low explosives through a slower combustion process known as deflagration."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/A_detonation_erupts_as_U.S._Marines_with_the_1st_Explosive_Ordnance_Disposal_Company%2C_Combat_Logistics_Regiment_2_conduct_a_demolition_operation_in_Helmand_province%2C_Afghanistan%2C_March_17%2C_2013_130317-M-KS710-206.jpg/330px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Explosion","wikidata":"Q179057"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c1/CastleBravo2.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c1/CastleBravo2.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"The explosion of the Castle Nectar nuclear bomb.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACastleBravo2.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/M1-67_%26_WR124.png/500px-M1-67_%26_WR124.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/M1-67_%26_WR124.png/1280px-M1-67_%26_WR124.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/M1-67_%26_WR124.png/500px-M1-67_%26_WR124.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The nebula M1-67 around Wolf–Rayet star WR 124 is the remnants of a stellar explosion, which is currently observed as six light years across[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AM1-67_%26_WR124.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Exploded_Electrolytic_Capacitor.jpg/500px-Exploded_Electrolytic_Capacitor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pars